

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 6

                                  FOR

                                  KAHN







          Lorenzo Cammoranesi
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  John II, King of Poland, after routing the Turks from Vienna in 1683 A.D.:
  "The immortal God... has blest us with so signal a victory as scarce the 
memory of man can equal.  Thanks be to Heaven, now the Half-Moon triumphs no 
longer over the Cross!"


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  With the coming of the spring season, Babba Sissoko (#0) prepared to 
quench his thirst for glory.  He informed Kahn that our former friendship 
has been rendered worthless by Kahn's outrageous provocations.

  Winter melted into spring, and Kahn made ready to carry out his urgent 
orders.  He cast a Flood spell and Peachwood was magically flooded.
  In early summer, Kahn moved into Gnarlia (#1301) with his high-spirited 
army.

  Soldiers carrying the battle-standards of the Kahnian empire marched on 
the Forest province of Gnarlia, a land defended by the soldiers of Fingol 
(#27).  Kahn commanded the attacking armies.  The defenders were led by 
Fingol.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Gnarlia (1301):

  144th   
  Legion  
 ннн06ннн 
          
  219th   
  Legion  
 ннн06ннн 
          
 142nd/C  
  Legion  
 ннн06ннн 
----------
 }}}27}}} 
 141st/A  
  Bowmen  
          
  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 218th Legion, the 143rd Light Cavalry, the 220th 
Light Cavalry and the 221st Light Cavalry in reserve.  Kahn stood ready at 
the head of his thousands.  Standing tall with his warriors was Fingol.
  A bad omen appeared, which dealt a telling blow to Kahn's fortunes.  Kahn
's mount was shot and killed while Kahn was giving a speech.  On the other 
hand Kahn maneuvered his troops against Fingol with great tactical foresight 
and obtained a tremendous tactical advantage.

  Across the entire front, the Crack 142nd Legion were arrayed against the 
141st Bowmen.  The 219th Legion and the 144th Legion flanked the undermanned 
enemy lines and charged in with full strength.  The 142nd Legion fought the 
141st Bowmen and squashed them like rotten tomatoes.
  The host of Kahn finally crushed the army of Fingol's morale with one last 
push.  The 142nd Legion destroyed the 141st Bowmen.
  Gnarlia was overrun by Kahn's forces in a hard-fought campaign.
  With the coming of the late summer season Kahn could not cast a Tornado 
spell because Kahn had already cast his allowed number of Element Magic 
spells.  So, Kahn tried hard to improve his Exploring, but he practiced in 
vain.
  Hawkins enlisted enough men in Gnarlia to create the 184th Bowmen and the 
188th Bowmen for the army of Kahn.
  During fall, Kahn marched on Sherwood (#1302) with his formidable command.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  Kahn invoked the Tome of Blessings, 
from which Sherwood was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected 
no armies in Sherwood.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Kahn for this year.


  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) has been informed by Kahn that his 
cooperation has become expendable, and therefore our previously friendly 
relations are now severed.
  Kahn treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Kahn treated with his ally 
Kwoth (#3).  Kahn treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).  Kahn treated with his 
ally Prometeo (#5).  Kahn treated with his ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Kahn 
treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Kahn treated with his ally Agesilao (#9).

  Here is the financial report for Kahn's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 33 gold in revenue.  6 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  
The 116th Garrison, the 184th Bowmen and the 188th Bowmen trained well and 
improved in quality.  19 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Kahn was 
left with 23 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Tattoo, Squire to Gladstone
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Gladstone looked for Isis in the taverns and inns of Kajaani.  
Gladstone encountered Isis (#89).  Chanting his artful words of magic into a 
great Mirror-Image Phantasm spell, Gladstone gestured with his arms and a 
second illusion of Isis sprang into existence!  Incanting a Telekinetic 
Storm spell, Isis directed glowing, interlacing strands of magic and damaged 
the illusion of Isis, inflicting 10 damage points.  The illusion of Isis's 
spell was disrupted by the event.  Some objects flew towards Isis and scored 
on her, inflicting 3 points of damage.  Isis disbelieved the illusion of 
Isis and it disappeared.  Chanting his words of magic with breathless 
precision, Gladstone let go a Spiritwrack spell, to make Isis quake and 
shiver with spiritual convulsions.
  Isis advanced to bow range.  Incanting a Holy Symbol spell, Gladstone 
channelled scintillating, writhing strands of magic.  A golden mist in the 
shape of a cross formed around Gladstone.
  Isis closed to melee range, filled with uncontrolled blood-lust.  Isis 
thrust at Gladstone with all her strength and inflicted 1 damage points on 
Gladstone.  Gladstone thrust at Isis but his aim was slightly off.
  Isis then swang at Gladstone with maximum force and inflicted 5 damage 
points.  Gladstone deftly swang at Isis and missed by a mile.  Isis circled 
left and violently attacked Gladstone but her sword whiffed through the air. 
Gladstone treacherously thrust at Isis and would have hit her if Isis hadn't 
ducked.  Isis swang at Gladstone but Gladstone evaded the blow.  Gladstone 
immediately swang at Isis but his aim was slightly off.
  Gladstone swang at Isis and walloped her with 6 damage points.  Seeking to 
take advantage of a gap in Gladstone's protection, Isis skillfully swang at 
Gladstone and missed badly.  Isis thrust at her vaunted nemesis but her 
sword whiffed harmlessly through the air.  Gladstone swang at Isis and would 
have hit her if Isis hadn't sidestepped just then.
  Isis swang at Gladstone but Gladstone evaded the sword.  Gladstone then 
swang at Isis with maximum force and damaged her, inflicting 2 damage 
points.  Isis contemptuously swang at Gladstone but her aim was just off.  
Gladstone circled right and violently attacked Isis and missed.  Isis thrust 
at Gladstone but her sword whiffed through the air.  Gladstone moved closer 
and thrust at Isis and scored on her, doing 6 points of damage.  Isis 
dropped to the ground, fatally pierced.  Thus did Isis die, a brave end by 
any standard.
  During early summer, Gladstone rode into Rejaf.  In his travels, he 
encountered no marauding monsters.
  Midsummer's day passed and late summer came.  Gladstone travelled to 
Damnonia.  He marched along an unusual route through Damnonia and raised our 
level of exploration there to 100%.  Gladstone was told by some sheepherders 
of a feature in Damnonia, a Tomb (#80) inhabited by the Ice Devil.  What 
treasure may lie there is unknown.  Legend has it that the Ice Devil is an 
extraordinarily cruel, cold and very powerful devil with magical powers.  In 
his travels, he saw no wandering monster.
  With the coming of the fall season Gladstone journeyed to Sherwood.  While 
adventuring, he encountered no monsters.
  In early winter, Gladstone girded his weapon and entered the Hollow Tree 
cautiously.  Gladstone encountered the Treant.  Gladstone hailed the Treant 
with words of greeting.  Sayeth Gladstone, "I have slain the vile Isis (#89).
No doubt the rascal hath passed to a plane of existence as dark and vile as 
Isis (#89)'s morbid soul!  Now that justice has been done, I claim the Large 
Hoard of Gold as my reward!"
  In its appreciation, the Treant swore off any raids in Sherwood.  Sayeth 
the Treant, "Yea, I have heard the news of thy deeds.  The bards shall sing 
of thy adventures for centuries to come.  Take then this Large Hoard of Gold 
as your reward.  Use it to cleanse the world of all evildoers!"  Gladstone 
extended his hands and thankfully accepted the Large Hoard of Gold from 
the Treant.  Gladstone bowed deeply, then departed from the Hollow Tree, 
head held high with pride in his worthy accomplishments.  He took 13 gold 
from the treasure of the Treant.
  While scouting the Hollow Tree, Gladstone saw a Crystal Ball which seemed 
to be of a magical nature.
  Magic runes formed on the Crystal Ball, saying "The Crystal Ball gives you 
the magic power to cast a Tornado spell.  The Tornado spell will take effect 
on this province as if a level-2 Elemental Mage had cast it.  1 skill 
level(s), chosen at random, will be drained from the character if the 
Crystal Ball is scouted.  You MUST have enough skill levels to meet the 
Crystal Ball's demand (to accept these terms, a character must give two 
Scout orders when Searching this feature."  During his travels this season, 
a Giant Wasp suddenly came at Gladstone like a bolt from the blue.  Chanting 
his artful words of magic into a mighty Spiritwrack spell, Gladstone 
gestured with his arms, to make the Giant Wasp quake and shiver with 
spiritual convulsions.
  The Giant Wasp loped along smoothly, conserving its energy, and closed to 
bow range.  Incanting a Holy Symbol spell, Gladstone directed scintillating, 
interlacing strands of magic.  A golden mist in the shape of a cross formed 
around Gladstone.
  The Giant Wasp charged into the melee.  The Giant Wasp treacherously 
thrust at Gladstone and damaged him, scoring 5 damage points.  Gladstone 
chanted the magic words for an Ice Suspension spell, but bit his lip on the 
last utterance and botched the spell.
  Gladstone turned around so as to flee from the Giant Wasp, but found that 
his retreat route had been magically blocked by a wall of shimmering force.  
The Giant Wasp thrust at Gladstone and walloped him with 2 damage points.  
Gladstone swang at the Giant Wasp and inflicted 5 damage points.  With 
amazing quickness, the Giant Wasp immediately thrust at Gladstone and scored 4
damage points on him.  Gladstone fell, mortally injured.  And so it came to 
pass that Gladstone met his unseemly end.


  Thy humble servant,   Tattoo, Squire to Gladstone


From: Hume
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I attempted a Bless spell, but bungled it.  My experience raised 
my prowess in White Magic.
  In early summer, I was instructed in the art of Sageness by Indra.  I 
practiced my Sageness and improved substantially.  I invented nothing in my 
sagely experiments.
  Midsummer's day came and went and a pleasant late summer came.  In my 
sagely researches, I discovered a fabulous invention called the Sextant!  
The following benefits are conferred by the Sextant:
  The Sextant allows the determination of a ship's position at sea.  Its 
effect is to raise the Naval ability of all of the generals of the Kingdom 
by 1 level.

  During fall, I invented nothing worthy of note in my sagely experiments.
  The fall season darkened into a frigid early winter.  I was instructed in 
the art of Druidism by Ishtar.  I practiced well and improved my skill in 
Druidism.

  Thy humble servant,   Hume


From: Charious
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I moved into Milo's Crossroads.  While on the march, I took an 
interest in the terrain of Milo's Crossroads, exploring some unknown 
territory.  We have now explored 100% of Milo's Crossroads.
  In early summer, I recruited enough men in Milo's Crossroads to form the 
116th Garrison for the army of the provincial garrison commander.
  Midsummer's day passed and a hot late summer came.  I rode into Rejaf.
  With the coming of the fall season, I travelled to Quantara Roo.
  Talking to some locals, I heard a rumor about a Desert Ruins in Abu 
Matariq (#106), occupied by the Chimera.  Some say that the Chimera owns the 
Large Hoard of Gold.
  In early winter, I cast a Bless spell.  Quantara Roo was magically blessed 
and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in Quantara Roo.

  Thy humble servant,   Charious


From: Frodo, Squire to Hawkins
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Hawkins explored Gnarlia carefully, leaving no stone unturned, 
and our exploration level there has risen to 23%.
  Hawkins heard a rumor telling of a feature in Damnonia (#1402) previously 
unknown to us, a Tomb inhabited by the Ice Devil.  The Tomb is reputed to 
contain the Large Hoard of Gold.
  The wet spring blossomed into a sultry early summer.  Hawkins's 
Clairvoyance spell fizzled and Hawkins wound up covered with psycho-kinetic 
slime.  A strange magical aura may have worked against his spell.
  With the advent of the late summer season, Hawkins enlisted enough men in 
Gnarlia to create the 184th Bowmen and the 188th Bowmen for the army of Kahn.
  During fall, Hawkins could not cast a Charm spell because Hawkins had 
already cast his allowed number of Psychic Magic spells.  Instead, Hawkins 
practiced his Illusions for months, but could make no progress.
  The fall darkened into the stillness of early winter.  Fingol (#27) 
informed Hawkins that he would not sell his services for less than 4 gold.

  Thy humble servant,   Frodo, Squire to Hawkins


